# Step 28: an extension's `cineris.exec` (docs/steps/28/answered.md, "The
# processes"), and the sandbox launcher's input it needs.
#
# Each rule of the program's start is broken here: its lookup (outside the
# workspace and the writable roots, a directory at a time, .exe, .cmd and
# .bat only on Windows), the line the permission engine reads and its
# decision, the launcher of the extension's own (write roots, the
# temporary directory, the network, every level), the look at protected
# paths around it, its environment and input, the shim's line for
# cmd.exe, and the launcher's input field.
#
# The breaks of code only Windows runs carry `os: windows`; run them on a
# runner with `gh workflow run try --ref <branch> -f os=windows
# -f command="mutate step-28-exec --jobs 2"`.

# ------------------------------------------------------------ the lookup

[break] runnable-taken-from-a-relative-path-entry
rule: A program is looked for only in the absolute directories of PATH: a relative entry names wherever the harness was started.
file: crates/cineris-base/src/program.rs
in: find_runnable_outside
find: .filter(|directory| directory.is_absolute())
replace: .filter(|_| true)
caught-by:
    cineris-base program::tests::a_runnable_inside_an_avoided_root_or_a_relative_directory_is_passed_over

[break] runnable-taken-inside-the-workspace
rule: A program named by its bare name is never one inside the workspace or a writable root, nor reached through one.
file: crates/cineris-base/src/program.rs
in: find_runnable_outside
find: && !passes_through(candidate, &avoid)
replace: && !passes_through(candidate, &avoid[..0])
packages: cineris-base, cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-base program::tests::a_runnable_inside_an_avoided_root_or_a_relative_directory_is_passed_over
    cineris-core::it ext_exec::a_program_in_the_workspace_or_behind_a_relative_path_entry_is_not_found

[break] runnable-shims-not-tried
rule: On Windows each directory is looked in for name.cmd and name.bat as well as name.exe.
file: crates/cineris-base/src/program.rs
in: find_runnable_outside
find: .flat_map(|directory| names.iter().map(move |name| directory.join(name)))
replace: .flat_map(|directory| names.iter().take(1).map(move |name| directory.join(name)))
caught-by:
    cineris-base program::tests::by_windows_rules_a_runnable_is_looked_for_a_directory_at_a_time

[break] runnable-ordered-by-extension-across-directories
rule: On Windows the search goes a directory at a time: a name.cmd in an earlier directory is taken before a name.exe in a later one.
file: crates/cineris-base/src/program.rs
in: find_runnable_outside
find: .flat_map(|directory| names.iter().map(move |name| directory.join(name)))
replace: .flat_map(|directory| names.iter().enumerate().map(move |(rank, name)| (rank, directory.join(name)))).filter(|(_, candidate)| is_program(candidate, windows)).min_by_key(|(rank, _)| *rank).map(|(_, candidate)| candidate).into_iter()
caught-by:
    cineris-base program::tests::by_windows_rules_a_runnable_is_looked_for_a_directory_at_a_time

[break] runnable-takes-any-extension
rule: On Windows a name with an extension is taken only when it is .exe, .cmd or .bat: nothing else of PATHEXT (.ps1, .vbs, .js) is ever run.
file: crates/cineris-base/src/program.rs
in: find_runnable_outside
find: Some(_) => return None
replace: Some(_) => vec![OsString::from(name)]
